INV-fuhin. ADR-0041 declares directness (direct / transitive /
undeclared) and ecosystem (stdlib / third_party) for the external
dependencies a project relates to, and a manifest declaration is the
most direct evidence of that relationship, yet only boundary nodes were
stamped: supply_chain_summary.external_dep counted every kind=dependency
declaration as directness `unknown` and ecosystem `unknown`, and the
registry text and spec claimed declarations were stamped. An external
declaration now gets directness `direct` and an ecosystem from
supply_chain.declaration_ecosystem: `third_party` (the manifest
declares a package to fetch), or `stdlib` for composer's platform
requirements (php, ext-*, lib-*, composer-plugin-api). A declaration
naming an in-tree package (INV-kutub, tier 1) is not external and gets
neither. The producers (toml_config, xml_config, json_config) read
manifests, never lockfiles. The strict xfail WI-ziruv shipped (#1902)
passes unmarked. Not changed: the js_module package stand-ins and the
Cargo/ruby/php boundary nodes that still read `unknown` (WI-hajag,
WI-tikar).

WI-gidid. The grammar-unavailable branch appended its warning to an
AnalysisRun that collect_analyzer_result then discards (only an
unskipped run is appended), so INV-pitab's write reached no consumer.
The append is removed and the warning names the distribution to
install (TreeSitterAnalyzer.grammar_distribution, WI-pakof) instead of
"the required tree-sitter grammar package". pass_silence.py and
ADR-0056 said such a pass has "no carrier in existence to stamp"; the
run exists and is discarded BY POLICY (WI-mamiv declined to route it),
and they now say so. Not changed: the 58 analyzer-specific copies of
the message, part of WI-bagor's retrofit of skipped_passes reasons.

Addresses INV-fuhin, WI-gidid.

